{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542861-fan-cofd-monsters-in-curseborne","id":1542861,"title":"[Fan] CofD monsters in Curseborne","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-29T03:31:42-07:00","id":1542861,"title":"[Fan] CofD monsters in Curseborne","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Note:</b> For ease of reference, I shorten <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> to <b>CoD </b>and <b>Curseborne</b> to <b>CB</b> in my posts. It\u2019s only fan conversion and nothing here is associated with White Wolf or Onyx Path official rulings and stances.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">It was going to happen sooner or later \u2013 so better start conversation sooner.<span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude0a</span> Fan conversion topic how to transplant at least part of C<b>hronicles of Darkness </b>splats/monsters ( Kindred, Uratha, Lost, Created, etc. ) to <b>Curseborne</b> setting.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So let\u2019s start\u2026</span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Easiest would be simply add 4<sup>th</sup> Character Path</b> \u2013 We have <b>Linage </b>( General Splat \u2013 vampire, werewolf, undead, etc. ), we have <b>Family</b> ( that is more like X-Splat of CoD \u2013 for <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b> there were <i>Deava, Gangrel, Mekhet, Nosferatu </i>and<i> Venture </i>\u2013 can be simply put like that in to <b>CB</b> ) and <b>Role</b> ( mortal world \u2018job\u2019 our CB monsters do. ) As we see, we do not have place for Y-Splat factions ( vampires Covenants, werewolves Tribes, mages Orders, etc. ) as those are \u2018eaten up\u2019 in <b>CB</b> to <b>Family </b>( Family basically doing dual X- and Y-Axis role in<b> C</b>B game). Adding 4<sup>th</sup> Path would just solve this issue easily.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>This leading me to maybe making 5 </b>Path char sheets alternatives, to have things likes Z-Axis also \u2013 ie. Bloodlines, Lodges, Legacies, etc. But it\u2019s just general idea.</span></span></li> </ol><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">But let\u2019s see how to maybe play with <b>only 3 Path</b> structure of original <b>CB</b> now\u2026<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">3. <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b> Kindred can simply works with Clans as Hungry Families \u2013 so Familes of <i>Deava, Gangrel, Mekhet, Nosferatu </i>and<i> Venture</i>, working more like Covenants politically. Fore ease of reference let\u2019s short assortations like that \u2013 remember it\u2019s much more shorthand and stereotype than direct translation. In the end, much better would be to have Covenants as 4<sup>th</sup> Path simply.</span></div><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Deava</b> \u2013 Carthian Movement?</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Gangrel</b> \u2013 Circle of the Corn</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Mekhet</b> \u2013 Ordo Dracul</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Nosfertau </b>\u2013 Lancea Sanctum</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Ventrue</b> \u2013 Invictus</span></li> </ul><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">4. <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken Uratha </b>werewolves would work with Auspices as Primals Families. They also work double role as 'hunting archetype\u2019'. So we have this associations:</span></div><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Rahu </b>(The Full Moon, The Warrior)</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Cahalith </b>(The Gibbous Moon, The Visionary) </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Elodoth</b> (The Half Moon, The Walker Between) </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Ithaeur </b>(The Crescent Moon, The Spirit Master) </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Irraka</b> (The New Moon, The Stalker)</span></li> </ul><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">5. <b>Changeling the Lost changelings</b> are, contrary, much simple to use. As changelings would simply by all Outcasts, whatever Kith or Seeming they are, we can flaten all the structures here. Go with more social role of Linage</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> and make changelings Courts simply Outcasts</span>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Families, with many different looking members of them. So new Outsiders Families to <b>CB</b> would be:</span></div><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Spring Court</b> - Focusing on hiding from the Fae by living amongst the mortals. They thrive on <i>Desire</i>.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Summer Court</b> - Seeking to strike out against the Fae directly. They thrive on <i>Wrath</i>.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Autumn Court</b> - Exploring the powers of faerie magic and the enigmas of the unknown. They thrive on <i>Fear.</i></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Winter Court</b> - Masters of deception and keepers of mysteries. They thrive on<i> Sorrow</i>.</span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">That\u2019s just my starting ideas, few days before <b>Curseborne </b>Kickstarter starting. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude0a</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-12-2024, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T03:56:14-07:00","id":1542863,"title":"","content":"If I wanted to play a game of Forsaken in CB I would probably replace family with tribe and make each tribe a full family path complete with its own 3 magics. Auspices would probably replace Lineage. Lodges I might have as optional role patches. This serves to get rid of the things they would all have in common otherwise, while allowing the most diversity, IMO. <br /> <br /> But 10 pathes isn't a huge undertaking in exchange for transplanting an entire game line. But if the goal is all splats suddenly renaming and a fourth path without mechanical benefits becomes more interesting because they will already have diversity in CBs rules and 10* splats in Chronicles is a lot of pathes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T12:36:04-07:00","id":1542875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542861-fan-cofd-monsters-in-curseborne?p=1542863#post1542863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But 10 pathes isn't a huge undertaking in exchange for transplanting an entire game line. But if the goal is all splats suddenly renaming and a fourth path without mechanical benefits becomes more interesting because they will already have diversity in CBs rules and 10* splats in Chronicles is a lot of pathes.</div> </div> </div> </div>One question - Where did you get 10 Paths? \ud83d\ude2e Basic X-Axis model of <b>CoD</b> would use normal 3 Paths per character of <b>CB </b>( with previous X-Axis - <i>Clan, Auspice, Mage Path</i> - being Family Path in <b>CB</b> ). To represent Social Factions Y-Axis ( <i>Covenant, Tribe, Order</i>, etc. ) best would to have 4th Path per character. Full translation you can make with max 5th Path per character - there you would have mechanics like <i>Bloodline, Lodge, Legacy</i>, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-12-2024, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T14:21:00-07:00","id":1542878,"title":"","content":"I should have said only 10 pathes requiring a significant amount of work. <br /> <br /> For Werewolf it would be Tribe replacing family and Auspice replacing lineage. There are 5 of each, that's a total of 10 that you actively need to create. In the core book Lodge has no mechanics, and it would be easy to say lodge can just be a role path, especially since role path is never a major path and doesn't being with it any special abilities, its just 4 attribute points and a selection of skills. <br /> <br /> Vampire does have more importance on covenant, so I would probably do clan and covenant with bloodline replacing role. It's not as clean as Werewolf, but it would be functional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T09:04:29-07:00","id":1543005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542861-fan-cofd-monsters-in-curseborne?p=1542878#post1542878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Werewolf it would be Tribe replacing family and Auspice replacing lineage.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you replace Linage with Auspice - you will have problems with shapeshifting powers etc. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T10:42:06-07:00","id":1543015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542861-fan-cofd-monsters-in-curseborne?p=1543005#post1543005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you replace Linage with Auspice - you will have problems with shapeshifting powers etc. \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>The shape shifting powers are a problem with or without lineage, there's only one other form assumed by default. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T20:40:40-07:00","id":1543387,"title":"","content":"Watching Inspiration Media proposed series <b><i>The Order</i></b> ( 2019 ) I got idea for werewolves. <b>Auspices</b> are still <b>Family</b> Path - however Tribal connections are from the Creature you change into. In TV series each werewolves 'Wolf Beast' is particular has it's own name and personality, related to various iteration of it around centuries. Marrying it with <b>Curseborne</b> and <b>CoD</b> setting, we got that each Uratha Creature is part of Firstborn cohorts - or IS small shared of the Firstborns themselves. You are not simply <b><i>Itheur</i></b>, you are <b><i>Itheur</i></b> with the soul of <b><i>Winter Wolf</i></b>, part of his Storm Lords children. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T02:50:10-07:00","id":1543505,"title":"","content":"In <b>Hungry</b> (vampires) preview chapter of CB there is mentioned legend of <i><b>Lazarus</b></i> - as first vampire in Golconda like change going from mortal to vampire - and to mortal again. So there is a nice thread to add in Lancea Sanctum as opposed faction to them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( As Lancea Sanctum is saying that vampires <i><b>sacred duty from God </b></i>is to be monsters. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-10-2024, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T15:55:20-07:00","id":1543554,"title":"","content":"The more I read <b>Curseborne</b> corebook, the more I think I would use <b>CoD </b>gamelines backstories as 'lore' &amp; myths of particular monster types. For example, Hungry Families more or less nicely translate to <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b> Clans- as Clans playing 'stories and myths' they told about themselves - and Family Paths of <b>Curseborne</b> for direct mechanics. Like this naming shorthenings:<ul><li><b>Deava</b> \u2013 House Bathory</li> <li><b>Gangrel</b> \u2013 ???</li> <li><b>Mekhet</b> \u2013 Ascetics</li> <li><b>Nosfertau </b>\u2013 Vorare ( only you need to change 'Flaming' effects to more 'Scarying' ones )</li> <li><b>Ventrue</b> \u2013 Heirs</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-11-2024, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T22:35:40-07:00","id":1543609,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Official podcast of Onyx Path on Who you can play in Curseborne. In first 20 minutes or so it is bluntly said that devs host Eddy and Matthew would be <b>glad if you want to recreate character ideas from other \u2018of Darkness\u2019 games in Curseborne</b>. For example, that is Outcast that is more or less changeling from <b>Changeling: The Lost</b>. ( Or closest analogue. ) I\u2019m validated then to run CB with CoD background setting. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude0e</span></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://onyxpathcast.podbean.com/e/episode-332-what-can-you-play-in-curseborne/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">https://onyxpathcast.podbean.com/e/episode-332-what-can-you-play-in-curseborne/</span></a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T07:07:53-07:00","id":1544098,"title":"","content":"6. With Sorcerers preview subchapter, I finally can compare <b>Mage: The Awakening</b> Orders to the Sorcerers Families:<ul><li><b>Adamantine Arrow</b> - No Family connection?</li> <li><b>Guardians of the Veil</b> - Faceless</li> <li><b>Mysterium</b> - Archivists ( after Keepers of the Word ) , Reeves ( after Panscryptias? )</li> <li><b>Silver Ladder </b>- Premiere</li> <li><b>Free Council </b>- Unburden (more communist ), Network ( more capitalistic )</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}